ted care, treatment planning, and scheduling to promote optimal oral health outcomes. Through effective communication, clinical expertise, and a commitment to disease prevention, this role contributes to a positive patient experience and the overall effectiveness of dental practice. Review and update medical histories and provide comprehensive preventive and therapeutic oral health care, including assessments, periodontal treatments, fluoride applications, radiographs, and patient/caregiver education. Collaborate with the dental team to support treatment planning and maintain precise detailed clinical documentation, ensuring high quality patient care. Support clinical operations by managing hygiene and clinical supplies, maintaining equipment and infection control protocols, ensuring OSHA and HIPAA compliance, and providing backup assistance with appointment confirmations and scheduling. Promote smooth clinic operations and a positive patient experience by collaborating with staff and trainees, maintaining a professional and welcoming environment, and demonstrating patient centered values that support the clinic’s mission. Travel to other clinics required. All other duties as required. What We're Looking For Basic Requirements: Knowledge and experience typically acquired by an Associate's Degree in Dental Hygiene. 1-3 years Clinical dental hygiene experience. Intermediate proficiency in dental practice management software and Microsoft Office applications. Dental Hygienist - Massachusetts State License. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree. Experience in treating patients with developmental, behavioral, or medical complexities. Pay Range Minimum $49.30, Midpoint $58.70, Maximum $68.10 Salary is based on related experience, expertise, and internal equity; generally, new hires can expect pay between the minimum and midpoint of the range. Apply Refer JOB_DESCRIPTION.SHARE.HTML CAROUSEL_PARAGRAPH JOB_DESCRIPTION.SHARE.HTML An employee in this position must comple